  <h2 id="introduction">Introduction</h2>
  <p>Recipes connect several parts of restaurant service in Karinderya. A customer order identifies the food being requested, ingredients support its preparation, Grocery helps organize supplies, and cooking turns those requirements into food that can be served.</p>
  <p>This hub brings those topics together without duplicating the individual category pages. Use the <a href="/food/">Food Directory</a> to browse the wider menu section, the <a href="/ingredients/">Ingredient Guide</a> for ingredient entries, and the <a href="/grocery/">Grocery</a> page for restocking information.</p>

  <h2 id="how-recipes-work">How Recipes Work</h2>
  <p>A recipe helps connect what a customer requests with the restaurant resources and cooking work needed to complete that order. The relationship can be read as:</p>
  <p><strong>Order → Ingredients → Cooking → Food → Serving</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Order:</strong> identifies the food requested by the customer.</li>
    <li><strong>Ingredients:</strong> connect the request with the supplies used by the restaurant.</li>
    <li><strong>Cooking:</strong> places the order into the kitchen workflow.</li>
    <li><strong>Food:</strong> represents the prepared order before it reaches the customer.</li>
    <li><strong>Serving:</strong> completes the restaurant workflow for that order.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="featured-content">Featured Content</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
